WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.320
Baker Street.

2
00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:03.360
Yellow fog at the window.

3
00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:06.970
A violin, a chemistry
rack, and a small bottle.

4
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:07.880
Days pass.

5
00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:10.100
The clock ticks faster.

6
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:11.660
Then, a knock.

7
00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:13.280
A card on a tray.

8
00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:17.420
The room fills with papers,
clues and a magnifying lens.

9
00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:18.810
Case closed.

10
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:22.980
The papers clear away, and a hand
reaches back towards the bottle.

11
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.870
Same bottle, first page and last.

12
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.570
Why would Doyle frame his hero like that?

13
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.720
In this mission, you'll
test Holmes's own excuse:

14
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:35.120
"My mind," he said,
"rebels at stagnation."

15
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:36.380
What does he mean?

16
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:38.930
You'll hear Watson object, as a doctor.

17
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.170
And you'll watch the reasoning machine
read a life from one old watch.

18
00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:47.660
Your mission: explain why the story
opens and closes with cocaine.
